file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge rotated to fold E, the prior edge demoted, the third folded away to the logs
recommend keep-going the other half of the printing carry is named and sized: `tell_the_reader` at 60 lines in 28 rungs and `tell_the_reopener` at 48 in 11, together 2,100 carried lines. Both read a run's own report through helpers each rung writes for itself, so they want fold D's `comptime` seam rather than this lap's whole-body lift -- the same seam, one tier deeper. Verify the reach of each symbol as `pub` before moving a line, exactly as this lap did, since that check is what made a 986-line edit safe.
